    "whatItTellsYou": "The curve pins down the lens's focal length: magnification blows up as the object nears u = f, and it passes through m = −1 (a same-size, inverted image) exactly when the object sits at twice the focal length, u = 2f — two features you can read straight off the plot to solve for f. For objects far beyond 2f the image is inverted and shrunken (|m| < 1), while inside f (not shown here) the magnification would turn positive, signalling an upright, magnified virtual image as in a magnifying glass.",
